# Testing

Tests are part of the implementation, not an afterthought.

## Test categories

Use appropriate combinations of:

- unit tests
- feature tests
- integration tests
- API tests
- database tests
- authorization tests
- workflow tests
- browser/end-to-end tests where justified

## Domain tests

Domain rules should be testable independently where practical.

Focus on behavior and invariants.

## Authorization tests

Every sensitive capability should have tests for:

- authorized access
- unauthorized access
- wrong role
- wrong district scope
- unauthenticated access

## Workflow tests

Test:

- valid transitions
- invalid transitions
- unauthorized transitions
- rejection behavior
- reassignment
- SLA behavior
- audit creation
- notifications
- callback payload validation
- callback signature validation

## API tests

Test:

- authentication
- authorization
- validation
- response contract
- pagination
- filtering
- errors
- versioning

## Security tests

Test important security boundaries.

Do not test only happy paths.

## Database tests

Verify important:

- constraints
- relationships
- uniqueness
- spatial behavior
- transactional behavior

## Regression

Every production bug should result in a regression test when practical.

## Test quality

Do not weaken or delete tests merely to make implementation pass.

If a test appears incorrect, identify why before changing it.

## Coverage

Coverage targets are project requirements, but coverage percentage alone does
not demonstrate correctness.

Prefer meaningful behavioral coverage.
